              "role": "assistant",
              "content": "# CSV Parser Function\n\n```python\nimport csv\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Union\n\n\ndef parse_csv(\n    file_path: Union[str, Path],\n    *,\n    delimiter: str = \",\",\n    encoding: str = \"utf-8\",\n    strip_whitespace: bool = True,\n) -> List[Dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Parse a CSV file into a list of dictionaries.\n\n    Each row in the CSV file is converted into a dictionary where the keys\n    are the column headers (from the first row) and the values are the\n    corresponding cell contents as strings.\n\n    Args:\n        file_path: Path to the CSV file to parse. Can be a string or a\n            ``pathlib.Path`` object.\n        delimiter: Field delimiter used in the CSV file. Defaults to ``,``.\n        encoding: Text encoding used to read the file. Defaults to ``utf-8``.\n        strip_whitespace: If ``True``, leading and trailing whitespace is\n            stripped from each cell value. Defaults to ``True``.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of dictionaries, one per data row in the CSV file. Each\n"
